/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-03T14:26:44Z","updated_at":"2026-02-03T14:26:44Z","body":"The rebase worked, but the documentation needs to be synced. Once that's rebased as well, it'll be good to go!\r\n\r\n> Autocompletes as int instead of Control.CursorShape, sadly, but it seems like this is a GDVIRTUAL limitation.\r\n\r\nYeah, this is unfortunately something enums have to deal with atm, so the documentation is stuck with the `int` designation as well. Not a blocker for this PR because it's a general limitation","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3841655800/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3938175766","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111819#issuecomment-3938175766","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111819","id":3938175766,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qu8sW","user":{"login":"MewPurPur","id":85438892,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NDM4ODky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85438892?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur","html_url":"https://github.com/MewPurPur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-21T04:58:31Z","updated_at":"2026-02-21T04:58:31Z","body":"> but the documentation needs to be synced\r\n\r\nI wasn't sure what this meant, I assumed you were referring to addressing KoBeWi's feedback.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3938175766/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4066794602","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111819#issuecomment-4066794602","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111819","id":4066794602,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7yZlxq","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-16T10:52:55Z","updated_at":"2026-03-16T10:52:55Z","body":"@MewPurPur What @Repiteo meant is that the CI is failing because the documentation you added is invalid: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/22250723577/job/64373772750?pr=111819\r\n\r\n```diff\r\nRunning --doctool to see if this changes the public API without updating the documentation.\r\nIf a diff is shown, it means that your code/doc changes are incomplete and you should update the class reference with --doctool.\r\n\r\n\r\ndiff --git a/doc/classes/Control.xml b/doc/classes/Control.xml\r\nindex 568d90f8..67146c43 100644\r\n--- a/doc/classes/Control.xml\r\n+++ b/doc/classes/Control.xml\r\n@@ -93,7 +93,7 @@\r\n \t\t\t</description>\r\n \t\t</method>\r\n \t\t<method name=\"_get_cursor_shape\" qualifiers=\"virtual const\">\r\n-\t\t\t<return type=\"int\" enum=\"Control.CursorShape\" />\r\n+\t\t\t<return type=\"int\" />\r\n \t\t\t<param index=\"0\" name=\"at_position\" type=\"Vector2\" />\r\n \t\t\t<description>\r\n \t\t\t\tVirtual method to be implemented by the user. Returns the cursor shape for the position [param at_position] in the control's local coordinates, which will typically be used while hovering over this control. See [method get_cursor_shape].\r\n@@ -425,7 +425,7 @@\r\n \t\t</method>\r\n \t\t<method name=\"get_cursor_shape\" qualifiers=\"const\">\r\n \t\t\t<return type=\"int\" enum=\"Control.CursorShape\" />\r\n-\t\t\t<param index=\"0\" name=\"position\" type=\"Vector2\" default=\"Vector2(0, 0)\" />\r\n+\t\t\t<param index=\"0\" name=\"at_position\" type=\"Vector2\" default=\"Vector2(0, 0)\" />\r\n \t\t\t<description>\r\n \t\t\t\tReturns the mouse cursor shape for this control when hovered over [param position] in local coordinates. For most controls, this is the same as [member mouse_default_cursor_shape], but some built-in controls implement more complex logic.\r\n \t\t\t\tYou can override [method _get_cursor_shape] to implement custom behavior for this method.\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor `get_cursor_shape`, the param is named `at_position` and not `position`.\r\n\r\nAnd for `_get_cursor_shape`, the return type is not properly registered as an enum. That would need to be fixed in the C++ code (if possible) for the docs to reflect it.\r\n\r\nThe docs XML is generated with `--doctool` and if it changes from what you wrote manually (which seems to be the case here), it shows you what is actually registered in ClassDB.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4066794602/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4067144296","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111819#issuecomment-4067144296","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111819","id":4067144296,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ya7Jo","user":{"login":"MewPurPur","id":85438892,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NDM4ODky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85438892?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur","html_url":"https://github.com/MewPurPur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-16T11:58:35Z","updated_at":"2026-03-16T17:35:35Z","body":"Oh, I'm sorry. I should have it fixed now.","author_associati